# Line endings are LF in this repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this, editing a file from a Windows script rewrites every line in it.
# Python's write_text opens in text mode, and text mode on Windows translates
# \n to \r\n, so a change of two hundred lines was committed as sixteen
# thousand insertions and sixteen thousand deletions. The content was right and
# the diff was unreadable, which is worse than it sounds: nobody can review a
# whole-file rewrite, so nobody does.
#
# eol=lf is what the checked-out working copy gets, not only what is stored.
# Both editors used here handle LF, and the pipeline writes LF already.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by the newline logic, because a byte in them is a byte.
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.parquet binary
*.zip   binary
*.ods   binary
*.xlsx  binary
